 ### SCENARIO-PHASE4-032
 **Description:** Running Exp 4024 either writes `blocked_arc_offline_env_unavailable` when the offline Arcade cannot load, writes `complete: fifth_game_no_solve_<game>_<reason>` when the selected new candidate does not advance a level, or writes `success: fifth_game_solved_<game>_at_action_N` only when the real offline environment reports a level counter increment after the committed action plan. A successful run MUST set `game_solved=true`, `real_env_confirmed=true`, `total_games_solved` to the monotonic ARC accuracy counter after the solve, record the selected new game and excluded solved games, and preserve the explore -> induce -> verify -> act trace that led to the confirmed level-up.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-033: ARC-AGI-3 ArcMemo Solve Transfer V5
+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4025 as an ArcMemo solve-loop transfer check over the new .372 content from Exp 4021 and Exp 4024. It MUST read the existing upstream artifacts instead of rerunning exploration, build the seeded arm from accumulated concept memory and the verified action traces already produced by the .372 search/explore-first solvers, compare that seeded solve cost against a cold-start baseline cost for the same content, and treat persistent memory as a win only when it demonstrably reduces future cost. The terminal artifact `results/experiment_4025_arcmemo_solve_transfer_v5.json` MUST include bare top-level fields `honest_verdict`, `solve_transfer_win`, `actions_cold`, `actions_seeded`, and `inference_substrate`, and SHOULD preserve induction-call counts, upstream citations, and per-content cost details used to compute the totals.
+
+### SCENARIO-PHASE4-033
+**Description:** Running Exp 4025 either writes `complete: arcmemo_v5_no_transfer_<reason>` when required upstream artifacts are missing, unconfirmed, or show no seeded cost reduction, or writes `success: arcmemo_v5_transfer_<actions_cold>to<actions_seeded>_actions` only when the summed .372 seeded arm uses fewer actions or fewer induction calls than the cold arm on the same Exp 4021 and Exp 4024 content. A valid artifact MUST report `solve_transfer_win` as a bare boolean, `actions_cold` and `actions_seeded` as bare integers, cite the upstream inference substrate, and keep the verdict terminal-prefixed without claiming that memory helped merely because concepts were stored.
